# SpectroMind v2.0 Coding Standards

## Language
- Primary: TypeScript (strict mode)
- Secondary: Python 3.11+

## TypeScript
- Use strict type checking
- Prefer interfaces over types for objects
- Use async/await, not promises
- Error handling: try/catch with typed errors
- Use 'use client' directive for client components

## Python
- Type hints required
- Use dataclasses for data structures
- Async/await for I/O operations
- Logging: use structlog or standard logging
- Follow PEP 8 style guide

## API Design
- RESTful principles
- Versioned endpoints (/api/v2/)
- JSON request/response
- Error codes: 400 (bad request), 500 (server error)
- Always return { success: boolean } in responses

## File Structure
- API routes: app/api/v2/{module}/route.ts
- Services: lib/services/v2/{ServiceName}.ts
- Components: components/{category}/{ComponentName}.tsx
- Types: lib/types/v2/index.ts

## Error Handling
- Always use try/catch blocks
- Log errors with context
- Return user-friendly error messages
- Never expose internal errors to client

## Testing
- Unit tests: Jest (TS), pytest (Python)
- Integration tests: Playwright
- Coverage: >80%

## Documentation
- JSDoc for TypeScript functions
- Docstrings for Python functions
- API documentation: OpenAPI/Swagger
- README files for complex modules

## v2.0 Specific Rules
- Always check service health before calling
- Use fallback methods when primary service unavailable
- Cache expensive computations (conformers, DFT)
- Log all v2.0 API calls with version tag
- Include metadata.version in all responses

